    longDescription: 'JSON to C# Classes generates complete C# POCO class definitions from a JSON sample — with configurable namespace, class name, and serialisation attributes for both Newtonsoft.Json and System.Text.Json. .NET developers use it to scaffold model classes from REST API responses in seconds instead of writing them by hand, and teams use it to ensure consistent property naming and attribute conventions across their data layer when consuming third-party web services.',
    howToUse: '1. **Paste** your JSON data into the editor.\n2. **Configure** options like Namespace, Class Name, and property attributes.\n3. **Generate** the C# code instantly.\n4. **Copy** the resulting classes into your .NET project.',
    commonErrors: '- **Invalid JSON**: Ensure your input is well-formed JSON.\n- **Complex Types**: Highly irregular JSON structures may require manual adjustment of generated types.',
